 ## Overview
-This family covers methods that decompose volumetric data into tetrahedral cells and render them by projecting these 3D primitives onto the 2D image plane, leveraging hardware-accelerated rasterization for compositing [S1, unofficial][S2][S4, S6, S7][S8, S9, S10, unofficial][S11][S12, unofficial][S14, S16]. It solves the problem of efficiently rendering unstructured tetrahedral grids by converting them into partially transparent 2D polygons that are sorted and composited back-to-front [S1, unofficial][S2][S4, S6][S8, S9, S10, unofficial][S11][S12, unofficial][S14, S16]. Unlike ray-casting methods that sample scalar fields, this approach uses explicit geometric projection and scan-conversion [S2][S4, S6, S7][S12, unofficial][S14, S16].
+Tetrahedral representation and traversal is a family of object-order volume rendering techniques that decompose volumetric data into tetrahedral cells, project them onto the 2D image plane, and rasterize the resulting polygons to leverage hardware-accelerated graphics pipelines [S1, S2, S4, S6, S7, S8, S9, S10, S11, S12, S14, S16, S17, S18]. It solves the problem of efficiently rendering unstructured tetrahedral grids by converting 3D geometric primitives into 2D fragments that can be composited in back-to-front order [S1, S2, S4, S6, S8, S9, S10, S11, S12, S14, S16, S17, S18]. Unlike [Tetrahedral Volume Rendering](820-tetrahedral-volume-rendering.md), which typically relies on ray casting, this family uses explicit geometric projection and scan-conversion [S2, S4, S6, S7, S12, S14, S16]. It differs from [GPU-based Projected Tetrahedra](7484-gpu-based-projected-tetrahedra.md) in that the core algorithm performs sorting and projection in software, whereas later variants offload these steps to the GPU [S4, S7, S12, S14, S16].
 
